    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "session", "producer"],
    "summary": "The Sex Pistols' drummer, from the Strand he formed with his schoolfriend Steve Jones in 1972-73 to the band's end in January 1978, and in every reunion since 1996. 'Quite late starters', he learned as the band took off, on Faces, Roxy Music, Free and Motown records: Kenney Jones, Paul Thompson, Simon Kirke, Al Jackson Jr. and Mitch Mitchell. Never Mind the Bollocks was cut with 'just guitar and drums': plain, hard 4/4, 'accenting everything that Steve was playing', the hat in quarters or eighths, the kick pushing the 'and's or in eighths, crashes on the 1 and short snare runs into the chorus. Later the Professionals, Bananarama's first album as producer, Chiefs of Relief, Edwyn Collins's band, Man-Raze."
  },
